{{!--
header-includes.hbs: the site's own additions to <head>, on every page.

What it is
  Leed's head partial, `leed/head.hbs`, renders this file first in <head>,
  before Leed's own stylesheet, metadata and scripts, on every page that
  calls it: the pages site-template.hbs wraps, Leed's unsubscribe pages, and
  the documentation and API pages. Those last are built on Leed's own
  documentation layouts, which call `leed/head.hbs` themselves and are NOT
  wrapped in site-template.hbs.

Why here and not in site-template.hbs
  A tag written in site-template.hbs reaches only the pages that template
  wraps, so the documentation set never gets it. Written here, it reaches
  both. That makes this the one place for anything that must be true on
  every page of the site, docs included.

Turning it on
  Nothing to set. There is no CMS flag and no plan tier: `leed/head.hbs`
  checks `templateExists "header-includes.hbs"`, so the file existing is what
  enables it. Delete it and nothing breaks.

What belongs here
  - a preload for a self-hosted web font, for a family Leed does not install
    itself (its bundled fonts need nothing here)
  - site verification metas (Google Search Console, Bing, and the like)
  - analytics and other site-wide scripts, deferred
  - theme-color, the web manifest, and PNG and touch icon fallbacks

What does not
  - Tags only one kind of page needs: they go in that page type's layout.
  - The description, canonical URL, Open Graph and Twitter cards, and the
    SVG favicon: `leed/head.hbs` already writes them from the page and from
    the company's settings. The favicon is the company favicon (`favicon`
    in the page data), uploaded in the CMS under Settings, General, so never
    add a second <link rel="icon"> for that SVG here.
  - Anything visible: this is <head>, so markup for the page body belongs in
    a layout or a partial.
--}}

{{!-- The browser's own chrome (the title bar on mobile, the tab strip in some
      browsers) takes these colors. They are the page ground, --brand-bg, in
      light and dark mode: a fully tinted bar competes with the page it
      frames.

      A meta cannot read a CSS variable, so these two values are written out
      and must be kept in step with --brand-bg in tailwind/site/theme.css by
      hand. Change the brand there, and change these with it. --}}
<meta name="theme-color" media="(prefers-color-scheme: light)" content="###THEME_COLOR_LIGHT###">
<meta name="theme-color" media="(prefers-color-scheme: dark)" content="###THEME_COLOR_DARK###">

{{!-- Examples. Each is commented out, so none of them renders; uncomment and
      fill in the one you need. A file they name must exist before the tag
      goes live.

  A self-hosted web font, for a family Leed does not install itself. Put its
  .woff2 files in src/static/webfonts/ and declare them with @font-face in the
  site's CSS; a preload here fetches the main one early. Never link a font
  host instead: those URLs log every visitor.

    <link rel="preload" href="/static/webfonts/<family>-regular.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>

  A search engine's site verification, with the token it gives you:

    <meta name="google-site-verification" content="<token>">

  A script every page runs, analytics for example. `defer` keeps it off the
  critical path; bump ?v= when a file of your own changes, since nothing
  fingerprints it:

    <script defer src="https://<analytics host>/script.js" data-domain="<your domain>"></script>
    <script defer src="/static/js/<your-script>.js?v=1"></script>

  A web manifest, and PNG icons for what the SVG favicon does not cover: older
  browsers, and the touch icon iOS uses for a home-screen shortcut. Name your
  files with your brand's prefix: the build deletes any leed-*.png, and
  favicon-* and logo-* under src/static/images/ belong to the CMS.

    <link rel="manifest" href="/static/<brand>.webmanifest">
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="32x32" href="/static/images/<brand>-icon-32.png">
    <link rel="apple-touch-icon" sizes="180x180" href="/static/images/<brand>-apple-touch-icon.png">
--}}
